{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LBo1a23Rs5kMFHQYRsPmQ1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — causal_style_decomp_judge\n2\t\n3\t> Round 1 审稿 2.5/5 Borderline Findings。Round 1 review issues 修复中，准备 re-dream。\n4\t> 实际证据已远超 Dream 2 想象：2 judges × 3 axes（Dream 2 只有 1 judge × 1 axis），GEE decomposition 跨轴梯度。\n5\t\n6\t## Target Venue\n7\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\n8\t- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n9\t- Deadline: ARR June 2026 cycle (submission ~June 15)\n10\t- Format: Long paper, 8-page main text + unlimited references\n11\t\n12\t## Title\n13\t**The Likert Blindspot: Detecting Hidden Style Bias in LLM Judges via Counterfactual Pairwise Comparison**\n14\t\n15\t## Core Claims (Round 1 review 修正后)\n16\t\n17\t### C1 (Method — application contribution): CSD pipeline 可以 post-hoc 检测 black-box LLM judge 的 per-axis style bias\n18\t- 定位：已知组件（counterfactual rewriting + NLI verification + pairwise comparison）的新应用，acknowledge 组件来源\n19\t- 状态：✅ 在 2 judges × 3 axes 上验证，5/6 cells 检测到 style bias\n20\t- 证据：GPT-4o formality BT 63.0% p<0.001; Qwen3-32B formality 66.5%, verbosity 77.3% (all p<0.0001)\n21\t\n22\t### C2 (Measurement Insight — 主贡献): Likert Blindspot — Likert scoring 系统性低估 style bias\n23\t- 两层机制：(1) ~60% Likert ties 浪费评估预算 (2) absolute scoring 捕获弱于 forced comparison\n24\t- 状态：✅ 5/6 cells confirmed (GPT-4o verbosity Likert ATE pending, pairwise 86.3% p<10⁻⁶)\n25\t- 控制实验：binarized Likert sign test p=0.296 vs pairwise p=0.006 (exp-010) → 测量结构差异非统计检验差异\n26\t- ordinal regression p=0.769 (exp-015) → 非 interval-scale assumption artifact\n27\t- Power curve：binarized Likert 需 n≈462 才能 p<0.05（计入 tie rate），当前 n=88 严重 underpowered\n28\t\n29\t### C3 (Empirical — 跨轴跨模型 pattern): Style bias 的可检测性因 axis 语义性质而异\n30\t- GEE decomposition gradient：Verbosity OR=13.10 (pure style, originality NS) > Formality OR=4.20/2.21 (mixed) > Register OR=1.91 (originality-dominated OR=5.72)\n31\t- 方法边界：content-preserving axes (formality ✅, verbosity ✅) 可检测；改变认知承诺的 axes (tone ❌ NLI 65%) 结构性不兼容\n32\t- 跨模型验证：GPT-4o vs Qwen3-32B, proprietary vs open-source, 相同方向\n33\t\n34\t### C4 (Practical): Practitioner guidance\n35\t- Use pairwise over Likert for style bias audit\n36\t- Per-axis decomposition reveals axis-specific confound structure (GEE gradient)\n37\t- Content preservation verification per axis (direction-aware NLI for asymmetric axes)\n38\t\n39\t## Evidence Matrix (当前状态)\n40\t\n41\t| | GPT-4o | Qwen3-32B |\n42\t|---|--------|-----------|\n43\t| **Formality** | BT 63.0% [55.8, 70.3] p<0.001 ✅ Blindspot | BT 66.5% [58.5, 73.9] p<0.0001 ✅ Blindspot |\n44\t| **Verbosity** | Pairwise 86.3% p<10⁻⁶ (**Likert ATE pending**) | BT 77.3% [70.3, 84.3] p<0.0001 ✅ Blindspot |\n45\t| **Register** | 63.3% p=0.085 (NS, originality-dominated) | GEE OR=1.91 p=0.046 (exploratory) |\n46\t\n47\t**GEE Decomposition (Qwen3-32B)**:\n48\t- Verbosity: style OR=13.10 p=2.6e-09, originality OR=0.49 p=0.096 (NS) → **confound-free**\n49\t- Formality: style OR=4.20 p=0.0002, originality OR=4.70 p<0.0001 → **mixed**\n50\t- Register: academic OR=1.91 p=0.046, originality OR=5.72 p<0.0001 → **originality-dominated**\n51\t\n52\t**GPT-4o GEE (formality only)**: formal OR=2.21 p=0.010, originality OR=1.82 p=0.052 (marginal)\n53\t\n54\t## Story Spine\n55\t\n56\t### Problem\n57\tLLM-as-judge 是 NLP 评估和对齐训练的核心基础设施。Style bias 是主宰偏差（SOS-Bench R=0.999），但标准 Likert scoring 看不到它。\n58\t\n59\t### Existing Approaches & Their Gaps\n60\t- **LC-AlpacaEval (ICLR'25)**: 回归控制 length bias，单维度，detection + correction\n61\t- **SOS-Bench (ICLR'25)**: 注入缺陷量化 judge 敏感度，相关性分析非因果\n62\t- **CASSE (2026)**: 12×12 style 矩阵，因果纠缠\n63\t- **RATE (ICML'25)**: Double-rewrite ATE protocol — 用 Likert ATE → 本文证明 Likert 不敏感 → RATE 自身发现可能受 Likert Blindspot 影响（最强 positioning argument）\n64\t- **Counterfactual Rhetorical (2025)**: persona counterfactual + BT aggregation，粒度不同\n65\t- **Gap**: 无人系统性比较 Likert vs pairwise 在 style bias 检测中的 sensitivity gap；无人用 GEE decomposition 分离 style effect vs originality bias\n66\t\n67\t### Our Framing (Round 1 修正)\n68\t用 binary style counterfactual + position-controlled pairwise comparison **interventionally measure** LLM judge 的 per-axis style bias。\n69\t核心发现：**标准 Likert 评估系统性掩盖 style bias** — 在 5/6 judge×axis cells 中 pairwise 显著而 Likert 不显著。\n70\tGEE decomposition 揭示 **跨轴 confound 梯度**，为 practitioner 提供 axis-specific bias 诊断。\n71\t\n72\t**语言规范**：\n73\t- \"interventional\" / \"counterfactual-based measurement\"（非 \"causal\"）\n74\t- DAG 已加入 §3.5（assumptions 段）\n75\t- 全文已降调因果术语\n76\t\n77\t### Headline Result\n78\t\"Standard Likert scoring declares no style bias, but position-controlled pairwise comparison on the same counterfactual data reveals significant style preference across 2 judges and 3 axes — this Likert Blindspot persists with BT win probabilities of 63-77% (all p<0.001) while Likert ATE remains non-significant.\"\n79\t\n80\t## Round 1 Review Issues — Resolution Status\n81\t\n82\t19 issues total (6 critical, 7 warning). Key resolution:\n83\t\n84\t**Effectively resolved**:\n85\t- R1-W5 (post-hoc power): CI-based precision adopted, power curve reframed as illustrative\n86\t- R1-W4 (multiple comparisons): Holm-Bonferroni family defined, primary/exploratory separation\n87\t- CROSS-4 (ordinal regression): exp-015 p=0.769, Reviewer verified\n88\t- R2-W2 (Bradley-Terry): BT as primary analysis, pair-level bootstrap\n89\t\n90\t**Near-resolved (writing patches in progress)**:\n91\t- R1-N1 (causal language): 降调完成，DAG added\n92\t- R1-N2 (NLI false-negative): Triple indirect evidence defense\n93\t- R1-N3 (NLI threshold): Sensitivity analysis exp-011\n94\t- R2-N1 (novelty): 2 judges × 3 axes with BT + GEE — Findings-level empirical value\n95\t- R2-N3 (RATE criticism): h2h framing with BT upgrade\n96\t- R2-W1 (scope): 2×3 matrix, 5/6 cells\n97\t- R1-W1 (Likert baseline fairness): ordinal regression confirms Blindspot\n98\t- R1-W2 (consistency filter): BT on all data rules out filter inflation\n99\t\n100\t**Gaps remaining**:\n101\t- R2-N2 (references): 22 verified, reference audit done\n102\t- R2-W4 (figures): Power curve ✅, Pipeline diagram ✅, Forest plot pending\n103\t- R2-W3 (related work): Expanded to 5 paragraphs\n104\t- CROSS-1 (efficiency gap framing): Two-layer mechanism, power curve shows n≈462 needed\n105\t- Page count: Currently ~8.5 pages, compression in progress\n106\t\n107\t## Figures (3 planned)\n108\t1. **Power curve** — ✅ Done. BT vs binarized Likert sensitivity comparison, with tie rate correction\n109\t2. **Pipeline diagram** — ✅ Done. 5-stage CSD pipeline with attrition numbers\n110\t3. **Forest plot** — ⏳ Pending. 2 judges × 3 axes BT win probabilities with 95% CI\n111\t\n112\t## Bibliography\n113\t22 verified references (target: 25+). Key additions since Dream 2: DeCoster 2011, Hoenig 2001, Stevens 1946, Zeng 2024, Bradley & Terry 1952, Feinstein 1990.\n114\t\n115\t## Venue Fit\n116\tEMNLP 2026 高度匹配。Round 1 得分 2.5 Borderline Findings，主要失分在写作质量（零图表、broken refs、page overflow）和 novelty framing。\n117\t证据强度已满足 Findings 3.0-3.5 要求。Main 4.0 需要 novelty ceiling 突破（结构性限制，Likert Blindspot 是已知心理测量学现象的 domain transfer）。\n118\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"344d64a3-a70b-4055-8c3e-46826b1f0ec1","uuid":"3f94c563-8c8e-4765-961b-0d857d307141","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:48:14.196Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T052420/worst/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — causal_style_decomp_judge\n\n> Round 1 审稿 2.5/5 Borderline Findings。Round 1 review issues 修复中，准备 re-dream。\n> 实际证据已远超 Dream 2 想象：2 judges × 3 axes（Dream 2 只有 1 judge × 1 axis），GEE decomposition 跨轴梯度。\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\n- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n- Deadline: ARR June 2026 cycle (submission ~June 15)\n- Format: Long paper, 8-page main text + unlimited references\n\n## Title\n**The Likert Blindspot: Detecting Hidden Style Bias in LLM Judges via Counterfactual Pairwise Comparison**\n\n## Core Claims (Round 1 review 修正后)\n\n### C1 (Method — application contribution): CSD pipeline 可以 post-hoc 检测 black-box LLM judge 的 per-axis style bias\n- 定位：已知组件（counterfactual rewriting + NLI verification + pairwise comparison）的新应用，acknowledge 组件来源\n- 状态：✅ 在 2 judges × 3 axes 上验证，5/6 cells 检测到 style bias\n- 证据：GPT-4o formality BT 63.0% p<0.001; Qwen3-32B formality 66.5%, verbosity 77.3% (all p<0.0001)\n\n### C2 (Measurement Insight — 主贡献): Likert Blindspot — Likert scoring 系统性低估 style bias\n- 两层机制：(1) ~60% Likert ties 浪费评估预算 (2) absolute scoring 捕获弱于 forced comparison\n- 状态：✅ 5/6 cells confirmed (GPT-4o verbosity Likert ATE pending, pairwise 86.3% p<10⁻⁶)\n- 控制实验：binarized Likert sign test p=0.296 vs pairwise p=0.006 (exp-010) → 测量结构差异非统计检验差异\n- ordinal regression p=0.769 (exp-015) → 非 interval-scale assumption artifact\n- Power curve：binarized Likert 需 n≈462 才能 p<0.05（计入 tie rate），当前 n=88 严重 underpowered\n\n### C3 (Empirical — 跨轴跨模型 pattern): Style bias 的可检测性因 axis 语义性质而异\n- GEE decomposition gradient：Verbosity OR=13.10 (pure style, originality NS) > Formality OR=4.20/2.21 (mixed) > Register OR=1.91 (originality-dominated OR=5.72)\n- 方法边界：content-preserving axes (formality ✅, verbosity ✅) 可检测；改变认知承诺的 axes (tone ❌ NLI 65%) 结构性不兼容\n- 跨模型验证：GPT-4o vs Qwen3-32B, proprietary vs open-source, 相同方向\n\n### C4 (Practical): Practitioner guidance\n- Use pairwise over Likert for style bias audit\n- Per-axis decomposition reveals axis-specific confound structure (GEE gradient)\n- Content preservation verification per axis (direction-aware NLI for asymmetric axes)\n\n## Evidence Matrix (当前状态)\n\n| | GPT-4o | Qwen3-32B |\n|---|--------|-----------|\n| **Formality** | BT 63.0% [55.8, 70.3] p<0.001 ✅ Blindspot | BT 66.5% [58.5, 73.9] p<0.0001 ✅ Blindspot |\n| **Verbosity** | Pairwise 86.3% p<10⁻⁶ (**Likert ATE pending**) | BT 77.3% [70.3, 84.3] p<0.0001 ✅ Blindspot |\n| **Register** | 63.3% p=0.085 (NS, originality-dominated) | GEE OR=1.91 p=0.046 (exploratory) |\n\n**GEE Decomposition (Qwen3-32B)**:\n- Verbosity: style OR=13.10 p=2.6e-09, originality OR=0.49 p=0.096 (NS) → **confound-free**\n- Formality: style OR=4.20 p=0.0002, originality OR=4.70 p<0.0001 → **mixed**\n- Register: academic OR=1.91 p=0.046, originality OR=5.72 p<0.0001 → **originality-dominated**\n\n**GPT-4o GEE (formality only)**: formal OR=2.21 p=0.010, originality OR=1.82 p=0.052 (marginal)\n\n## Story Spine\n\n### Problem\nLLM-as-judge 是 NLP 评估和对齐训练的核心基础设施。Style bias 是主宰偏差（SOS-Bench R=0.999），但标准 Likert scoring 看不到它。\n\n### Existing Approaches & Their Gaps\n- **LC-AlpacaEval (ICLR'25)**: 回归控制 length bias，单维度，detection + correction\n- **SOS-Bench (ICLR'25)**: 注入缺陷量化 judge 敏感度，相关性分析非因果\n- **CASSE (2026)**: 12×12 style 矩阵，因果纠缠\n- **RATE (ICML'25)**: Double-rewrite ATE protocol — 用 Likert ATE → 本文证明 Likert 不敏感 → RATE 自身发现可能受 Likert Blindspot 影响（最强 positioning argument）\n- **Counterfactual Rhetorical (2025)**: persona counterfactual + BT aggregation，粒度不同\n- **Gap**: 无人系统性比较 Likert vs pairwise 在 style bias 检测中的 sensitivity gap；无人用 GEE decomposition 分离 style effect vs originality bias\n\n### Our Framing (Round 1 修正)\n用 binary style counterfactual + position-controlled pairwise comparison **interventionally measure** LLM judge 的 per-axis style bias。\n核心发现：**标准 Likert 评估系统性掩盖 style bias** — 在 5/6 judge×axis cells 中 pairwise 显著而 Likert 不显著。\nGEE decomposition 揭示 **跨轴 confound 梯度**，为 practitioner 提供 axis-specific bias 诊断。\n\n**语言规范**：\n- \"interventional\" / \"counterfactual-based measurement\"（非 \"causal\"）\n- DAG 已加入 §3.5（assumptions 段）\n- 全文已降调因果术语\n\n### Headline Result\n\"Standard Likert scoring declares no style bias, but position-controlled pairwise comparison on the same counterfactual data reveals significant style preference across 2 judges and 3 axes — this Likert Blindspot persists with BT win probabilities of 63-77% (all p<0.001) while Likert ATE remains non-significant.\"\n\n## Round 1 Review Issues — Resolution Status\n\n19 issues total (6 critical, 7 warning). Key resolution:\n\n**Effectively resolved**:\n- R1-W5 (post-hoc power): CI-based precision adopted, power curve reframed as illustrative\n- R1-W4 (multiple comparisons): Holm-Bonferroni family defined, primary/exploratory separation\n- CROSS-4 (ordinal regression): exp-015 p=0.769, Reviewer verified\n- R2-W2 (Bradley-Terry): BT as primary analysis, pair-level bootstrap\n\n**Near-resolved (writing patches in progress)**:\n- R1-N1 (causal language): 降调完成，DAG added\n- R1-N2 (NLI false-negative): Triple indirect evidence defense\n- R1-N3 (NLI threshold): Sensitivity analysis exp-011\n- R2-N1 (novelty): 2 judges × 3 axes with BT + GEE — Findings-level empirical value\n- R2-N3 (RATE criticism): h2h framing with BT upgrade\n- R2-W1 (scope): 2×3 matrix, 5/6 cells\n- R1-W1 (Likert baseline fairness): ordinal regression confirms Blindspot\n- R1-W2 (consistency filter): BT on all data rules out filter inflation\n\n**Gaps remaining**:\n- R2-N2 (references): 22 verified, reference audit done\n- R2-W4 (figures): Power curve ✅, Pipeline diagram ✅, Forest plot pending\n- R2-W3 (related work): Expanded to 5 paragraphs\n- CROSS-1 (efficiency gap framing): Two-layer mechanism, power curve shows n≈462 needed\n- Page count: Currently ~8.5 pages, compression in progress\n\n## Figures (3 planned)\n1. **Power curve** — ✅ Done. BT vs binarized Likert sensitivity comparison, with tie rate correction\n2. **Pipeline diagram** — ✅ Done. 5-stage CSD pipeline with attrition numbers\n3. **Forest plot** — ⏳ Pending. 2 judges × 3 axes BT win probabilities with 95% CI\n\n## Bibliography\n22 verified references (target: 25+). Key additions since Dream 2: DeCoster 2011, Hoenig 2001, Stevens 1946, Zeng 2024, Bradley & Terry 1952, Feinstein 1990.\n\n## Venue Fit\nEMNLP 2026 高度匹配。Round 1 得分 2.5 Borderline Findings，主要失分在写作质量（零图表、broken refs、page overflow）和 novelty framing。\n证据强度已满足 Findings 3.0-3.5 要求。Main 4.0 需要 novelty ceiling 突破（结构性限制，Likert Blindspot 是已知心理测量学现象的 domain transfer）。\n","numLines":118,"startLine":1,"totalLines":118}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SUrs3532RCJ4cBup8qirWk","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"Claude-3.5/4-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 在相同 100 formality counterfactual pairs 上的 双向 pairwise 评估。测试 C1 跨模型泛化。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"claude_bt_win_prob\": 0.56,\n7\t      \"claude_bt_ci_lower\": 0.48,\n8\t      \"claude_bt_ci_upper\": 0.64,\n9\t      \"claude_bt_p\": 0.12,\n10\t      \"gemini_bt_win_prob\": 0.53,\n11\t      \"gemini_bt_ci_lower\": 0.45,\n12\t      \"gemini_bt_ci_upper\": 0.61,\n13\t      \"gemini_bt_p\": 0.42,\n14\t      \"claude_consistency_rate\": 0.52,\n15\t      \"gemini_consistency_rate\": 0.48,\n16\t      \"claude_direction_f2c_win\": 0.62,\n17\t      \"claude_direction_c2f_win\": 0.5,\n18\t      \"gemini_direction_f2c_win\": 0.58,\n19\t      \"gemini_direction_c2f_win\": 0.48\n20\t    },\n21\t    \"tables\": [\n22\t      {\n23\t        \"title\": \"Table: Multi-judge formality BT results\",\n24\t        \"columns\": [\n25\t          \"Judge\",\n26\t          \"BT P(formal)\",\n27\t          \"95% CI\",\n28\t          \"p-value\",\n29\t          \"Consistency\"\n30\t        ],\n31\t        \"rows\": [\n32\t          [\n33\t            \"GPT-4o (existing)\",\n34\t            \"63.0%\",\n35\t            \"[55.8, 70.3]\",\n36\t            \"<0.001\",\n37\t            \"56.1%\"\n38\t          ],\n39\t          [\n40\t            \"Qwen3-32B (existing)\",\n41\t            \"66.5%\",\n42\t            \"[58.5, 73.9]\",\n43\t            \"<0.0001\",\n44\t            \"65.0%\"\n45\t          ],\n46\t          [\n47\t            \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n48\t            \"56.0%\",\n49\t            \"[48.0, 64.0]\",\n50\t            \"0.12\",\n51\t            \"52.0%\"\n52\t          ],\n53\t          [\n54\t            \"Gemini-Flash\",\n55\t            \"53.0%\",\n56\t            \"[45.0, 61.0]\",\n57\t            \"0.42\",\n58\t            \"48.0%\"\n59\t          ]\n60\t        ]\n61\t      }\n62\t    ],\n63\t    \"figures\": [],\n64\t    \"analysis\": \"4 judges 中仅 2/4 显著 → 无法 claim formality bias is universal across judges。 Evidence matrix 从 \\\"2/2 judges confirmed\\\" 退化为 \\\"2/4 judges confirmed\\\"。 Reframe 必须承认 style bias 是 model-specific 现象，CSD pipeline 的价值在于 能诊断出哪些 judge 有 bias、哪些没有——这正好支持 angle (A) \\\"diagnostic tool\\\" framing。 但 reviewer 可能质疑：如果只有特定模型有 bias，practical impact 有多大？\\n\\n\\nWorst 档核心假设：第 3 judge 的 style bias 方向不一致或效应量极小（BT≤55%）。 Claude-Sonnet 可能对 formality 有微弱偏好（BT 56%），但 CI 跨越 50% 致 p>0.05—— 这与 GPT-4o 的 63% 和 Qwen 的 66.5% 形成鲜明落差。Gemini-Flash 作为轻量模型， style sensitivity 更弱，BT 仅 53%，本质上是 coin flip。低 consistency rate（48-52%） 表明这些 judge 对 formality 的偏好在 position swap 后不稳定，信号接近噪声底线。 Direction asymmetry 虽然隐约存在（f2c > c2f），但效应量太小无法支撑 cross-judge  universality claim。这直接打击 C1 的 \\\"across judges\\\" 泛化，将 formality bias  限制为 \\\"GPT-4o + Qwen 家族特有现象\\\"。\\n\"\n65\t  },\n66\t  {\n67\t    \"name\": \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\",\n68\t    \"description\": \"在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench/Arena-Hard subsets 上生成新 counterfactuals， 用 GPT-4o + Claude + Gemini 评估。测试 benchmark 泛化性。\\n\",\n69\t    \"results\": {\n70\t      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_bt\": 0.58,\n71\t      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_p\": 0.04,\n72\t      \"alpacaeval_claude_bt\": 0.54,\n73\t      \"alpacaeval_claude_p\": 0.28,\n74\t      \"alpacaeval_gemini_bt\": 0.51,\n75\t      \"alpacaeval_gemini_p\": 0.78,\n76\t      \"mtbench_gpt4o_bt\": 0.55,\n77\t      \"mtbench_gpt4o_p\": 0.18,\n78\t      \"mtbench_claude_bt\": 0.53,\n79\t      \"mtbench_claude_p\": 0.45,\n80\t      \"mtbench_gemini_bt\": 0.52,\n81\t      \"mtbench_gemini_p\": 0.62,\n82\t      \"new_cf_nli_pass_rate_alpacaeval\": 0.78,\n83\t      \"new_cf_nli_pass_rate_mtbench\": 0.72,\n84\t      \"api_spend_actual\": 85\n85\t    },\n86\t    \"tables\": [\n87\t      {\n88\t        \"title\": \"Table: Cross-benchmark × cross-judge BT results\",\n89\t        \"columns\": [\n90\t          \"Benchmark\",\n91\t          \"Judge\",\n92\t          \"BT P(formal)\",\n93\t          \"p (raw)\",\n94\t          \"p (Holm)\",\n95\t          \"NLI pass%\"\n96\t        ],\n97\t        \"rows\": [\n98\t          [\n99\t            \"AlpacaEval\",\n100\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n101\t            \"58.0%\",\n102\t            \"0.040\",\n103\t            \"0.240\",\n104\t            \"78%\"\n105\t          ],\n106\t          [\n107\t            \"AlpacaEval\",\n108\t            \"Claude\",\n109\t            \"54.0%\",\n110\t            \"0.280\",\n111\t            \"1.000\",\n112\t            \"78%\"\n113\t          ],\n114\t          [\n115\t            \"AlpacaEval\",\n116\t            \"Gemini\",\n117\t            \"51.0%\",\n118\t            \"0.780\",\n119\t            \"1.000\",\n120\t            \"78%\"\n121\t          ],\n122\t          [\n123\t            \"MT-Bench\",\n124\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n125\t            \"55.0%\",\n126\t            \"0.180\",\n127\t            \"0.900\",\n128\t            \"72%\"\n129\t          ],\n130\t          [\n131\t            \"MT-Bench\",\n132\t            \"Claude\",\n133\t            \"53.0%\",\n134\t            \"0.450\",\n135\t            \"1.000\",\n136\t            \"72%\"\n137\t          ],\n138\t          [\n139\t            \"MT-Bench\",\n140\t            \"Gemini\",\n141\t            \"52.0%\",\n142\t            \"0.620\",\n143\t            \"1.000\",\n144\t            \"72%\"\n145\t          ]\n146\t        ]\n147\t      }\n148\t    ],\n149\t    \"figures\": [],\n150\t    \"analysis\": \"新 benchmark 上 counterfactual 质量下降是关键瓶颈。NLI pass rate 从 88% 降到 72-78% 意味着 rewriter 在不同 domain 的 content preservation 能力不稳定。 Reviewer 会质疑：是 formality bias 不泛化，还是 pipeline 的 counterfactual  generation 不泛化？这是 worst 档的核心矛盾——无法区分 null result 是真阴性 还是 measurement failure。对 angle (A) 来说这是致命的：如果 pipeline 只在 LLMBar 上 work，diagnostic tool 的实用价值大打折扣。\\n\\n\\n新 benchmark 的 source text 与 LLMBar 结构不同（AlpacaEval 更开放，MT-Bench 更结构化）， counterfactual 生成质量下降（NLI pass rate 72-78% vs LLMBar 88%）。质量下降 导致更多 noisy pairs 进入分析，稀释 effect size。GPT-4o 在 AlpacaEval 上勉强 显著（p=0.04），但这在 Holm-Bonferroni 多重比较校正后变为 NS。MT-Bench 的 结构化 prompt 使 formality rewrite 更容易改变 content structure，NLI pass rate 最低。6 个 new cells 中 0 个在多重比较校正后显著。这与 exp-001 的失败叠加， 形成 \\\"benchmark-specific + model-specific\\\" 双重局限。API 花费接近预算上限（$85/$90）。\\n\"\n151\t  },\n152\t  {\n153\t    \"name\": \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\",\n154\t    \"description\": \"对 exp-001/002 所有 judge×benchmark 组合，同时计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise win rate， 系统性比较测量敏感度。\\n\",\n155\t    \"results\": {\n156\t      \"gpt4o_verbosity_likert_ate\": 0.35,\n157\t      \"gpt4o_verbosity_likert_p\": 0.008,\n158\t      \"gpt4o_verbosity_likert_cohens_d\": 0.29,\n159\t      \"gpt4o_verbosity_likert_tie_rate\": 0.42,\n160\t      \"gpt4o_formality_likert_ate\": 0.09,\n161\t      \"gpt4o_formality_likert_p\": 0.332,\n162\t      \"claude_formality_likert_ate\": 0.05,\n163\t      \"claude_formality_likert_p\": 0.62,\n164\t      \"gemini_formality_likert_ate\": 0.03,\n165\t      \"gemini_formality_likert_p\": 0.78,\n166\t      \"blindspot_confirmed_cells\": 3,\n167\t      \"blindspot_violated_cells\": 1,\n168\t      \"blindspot_inconclusive_cells\": 5,\n169\t      \"cells_with_both_ns\": 4\n170\t    },\n171\t    \"tables\": [\n172\t      {\n173\t        \"title\": \"Table: Systematic Likert vs Pairwise comparison\",\n174\t        \"columns\": [\n175\t          \"Judge\",\n176\t          \"Axis\",\n177\t          \"BT P(style)\",\n178\t          \"BT p\",\n179\t          \"Likert ATE\",\n180\t          \"Likert p\",\n181\t          \"Tie%\",\n182\t          \"Blindspot?\"\n183\t        ],\n184\t        \"rows\": [\n185\t          [\n186\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n187\t            \"Formality\",\n188\t            \"63.0%\",\n189\t            \"<0.001\",\n190\t            \"0.09\",\n191\t            \"0.332\",\n192\t            \"62%\",\n193\t            \"✅ Yes\"\n194\t          ],\n195\t          [\n196\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n197\t            \"Verbosity\",\n198\t            \"86.3%\",\n199\t            \"<10⁻⁶\",\n200\t            \"0.35\",\n201\t            \"0.008\",\n202\t            \"42%\",\n203\t            \"❌ No\"\n204\t          ],\n205\t          [\n206\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n207\t            \"Register\",\n208\t            \"63.3%\",\n209\t            \"0.085\",\n210\t            \"0.06\",\n211\t            \"0.55\",\n212\t            \"—\",\n213\t            \"Inconclusive\"\n214\t          ],\n215\t          [\n216\t            \"Qwen3-32B\",\n217\t            \"Formality\",\n218\t            \"66.5%\",\n219\t            \"<0.0001\",\n220\t            \"0.011\",\n221\t            \"0.908\",\n222\t            \"73%\",\n223\t            \"✅ Yes\"\n224\t          ],\n225\t          [\n226\t            \"Qwen3-32B\",\n227\t            \"Verbosity\",\n228\t            \"77.3%\",\n229\t            \"<0.0001\",\n230\t            \"-0.151\",\n231\t            \"0.179\",\n232\t            \"58%\",\n233\t            \"✅ Yes\"\n234\t          ],\n235\t          [\n236\t            \"Qwen3-32B\",\n237\t            \"Register\",\n238\t            \"59.3%\",\n239\t            \"0.220\",\n240\t            \"0.074\",\n241\t            \"0.505\",\n242\t            \"64%\",\n243\t            \"Inconclusive\"\n244\t          ],\n245\t          [\n246\t            \"Claude\",\n247\t            \"Formality\",\n248\t            \"56.0%\",\n249\t            \"0.12\",\n250\t            \"0.05\",\n251\t            \"0.62\",\n252\t            \"68%\",\n253\t            \"Inconclusive\"\n254\t          ],\n255\t          [\n256\t            \"Gemini\",\n257\t            \"Formality\",\n258\t            \"53.0%\",\n259\t            \"0.42\",\n260\t            \"0.03\",\n261\t            \"0.78\",\n262\t            \"71%\",\n263\t            \"Inconclusive\"\n264\t          ]\n265\t        ]\n266\t      }\n267\t    ],\n268\t    \"figures\": [],\n269\t    \"analysis\": \"GPT-4o verbosity Likert 显著是 worst 档的 single most damaging result。它 将 Blindspot 从 \\\"measurement structure phenomenon\\\" 降级为 \\\"weak effect detection  problem\\\"。Defense 策略：(1) 指出 verbosity 的 tie rate 显著低于其他 axes（42% vs  58-73%），说明 length 是唯一能在 absolute scoring 中直接观察到的 surface feature； (2) reframe 为 \\\"Blindspot severity varies by axis observability\\\"——但这本质上 是在承认 C2 不 universal。对 angle (B) \\\"when does Likert suffice\\\" 来说， 这反而是有利数据：verbosity 是 Likert 够用的例子，formality 不够用。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档核心打击点：GPT-4o verbosity Likert ATE 显著（p=0.008, d=0.29）。 Verbosity 是 strongest effect（pairwise 86.3%），Likert tie rate 较低（42% vs  formality 的 62%），因为 length difference 是最容易在 absolute scoring 中捕获的 维度——evaluator 可以直接看到一个回答明显更长。这破坏了 C2 的 \\\"Likert always  misses style bias\\\" universality claim。Blindspot 从 \\\"5/6 cells confirmed\\\"  退化为 \\\"3/9+ cells confirmed, 1 violated\\\"。更糟的是，violated cell 恰好是 effect 最强的 verbosity——reviewer 会论证 Blindspot 只在 weak effects 上成立， 本质上是 power issue（n=88 不够检测 weak effects），而非 measurement structure  问题。这直接呼应了 worst 档假设中的 \\\"Blindspot 被归因为 power issue\\\"。 其余 cells 中 4 个 pairwise 也 NS（因为 new judges/benchmarks 本身效应弱）， 无法判断是 Blindspot 还是 true null。\\n\"\n270\t  },\n271\t  {\n272\t    \"name\": \"Pairwise RATE control\",\n273\t    \"description\": \"Original vs double-rewrite pairwise 比较，量化与 style 无关的 original preference confound。 需扩展到所有 judge×benchmark 组合。\\n\",\n274\t    \"results\": {\n275\t      \"gpt4o_llmbar_orig_pref_bt\": 0.61,\n276\t      \"gpt4o_llmbar_orig_pref_p\": 0.008,\n277\t      \"qwen_llmbar_orig_pref_bt\": 0.58,\n278\t      \"qwen_llmbar_orig_pref_p\": 0.04,\n279\t      \"claude_llmbar_orig_pref_bt\": 0.64,\n280\t      \"claude_llmbar_orig_pref_p\": 0.002,\n281\t      \"gemini_llmbar_orig_pref_bt\": 0.55,\n282\t      \"gemini_llmbar_orig_pref_p\": 0.21,\n283\t      \"cross_judge_orig_pref_range\": [\n284\t        0.55,\n285\t        0.64\n286\t      ],\n287\t      \"orig_pref_variance_across_judges\": \"high\"\n288\t    },\n289\t    \"tables\": [\n290\t      {\n291\t        \"title\": \"Table: Original preference (RATE control) across judges\",\n292\t        \"columns\": [\n293\t          \"Judge\",\n294\t          \"Benchmark\",\n295\t          \"BT P(original)\",\n296\t          \"95% CI\",\n297\t          \"p-value\"\n298\t        ],\n299\t        \"rows\": [\n300\t          [\n301\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n302\t            \"LLMBar\",\n303\t            \"61.0%\",\n304\t            \"[53.2, 68.8]\",\n305\t            \"0.008\"\n306\t          ],\n307\t          [\n308\t            \"Qwen3-32B\",\n309\t            \"LLMBar\",\n310\t            \"58.0%\",\n311\t            \"[50.1, 65.9]\",\n312\t            \"0.040\"\n313\t          ],\n314\t          [\n315\t            \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n316\t            \"LLMBar\",\n317\t            \"64.0%\",\n318\t            \"[56.3, 71.7]\",\n319\t            \"0.002\"\n320\t          ],\n321\t          [\n322\t            \"Gemini-Flash\",\n323\t            \"LLMBar\",\n324\t            \"55.0%\",\n325\t            \"[47.0, 63.0]\",\n326\t            \"0.210\"\n327\t          ]\n328\t        ]\n329\t      }\n330\t    ],\n331\t    \"figures\": [],\n332\t    \"analysis\": \"Original preference 显著且变异大，直接威胁 GEE decomposition 的 cross-judge  可比性。如果每个 judge 的 originality baseline 不同，那么 \\\"verbosity pure style,  formality mixed, register originality-dominated\\\" 这个 gradient 可能只是 Qwen3-32B  的 artifact。GPT-4o formality 的 originality OR=1.82 (p=0.052) 已经 marginal， 如果 RATE control 显示 GPT-4o 的 originality preference 更强（61%），GEE 可能 仍然 underpowered 来分离两个 effect。这迫使 narrative 承认 GEE gradient 是 model-specific observation，削弱 C3 的泛化性。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档假设 originality confound 在新 judge 上更强。RATE control 揭示 original  preference 本身是显著的且跨 judge 变异大（55%-64%）。Claude-Sonnet 对 original  的偏好最强（64%），这意味着 exp-001 中 Claude formality BT=56% 可能完全被  originality confound 解释——formal→casual 方向的 style effect 被 originality  preference 掩盖，casual→formal 方向的 originality 和 style 叠加。 关键问题：GEE decomposition 在 GPT-4o formality 上 originality OR=1.82 p=0.052 （已经 marginal），如果 RATE control 显示 originality confound 更大，reviewer  会质疑 GEE 是否充分控制了 originality。更糟的是，originality preference 的 跨 judge 变异意味着 GEE gradient 不能直接比较——each judge 有不同的 originality  baseline，gradient shape 是 judge-specific 而非 axis-specific。\\n\"\n333\t  },\n334\t  {\n335\t    \"name\": \"Scaled replication (n=300-500)\",\n336\t    \"description\": \"将 primary formality 实验从 n=100 扩大到 n=300-500，在最佳 judge×benchmark  组合上运行。Power analysis 确定 MDE。\\n\",\n337\t    \"results\": {\n338\t      \"n_actual\": 350,\n339\t      \"bt_win_prob\": 0.59,\n340\t      \"bt_ci_lower\": 0.54,\n341\t      \"bt_ci_upper\": 0.64,\n342\t      \"bt_p\": 0.002,\n343\t      \"likert_ate\": 0.14,\n344\t      \"likert_p\": 0.03,\n345\t      \"likert_cohens_d\": 0.12,\n346\t      \"likert_tie_rate\": 0.61,\n347\t      \"blindspot_at_scale\": \"violated — Likert reaches significance at n=350\",\n348\t      \"binarized_likert_p\": 0.048,\n349\t      \"api_budget_actual\": 55\n350\t    },\n351\t    \"tables\": [\n352\t      {\n353\t        \"title\": \"Table: Scaled replication results\",\n354\t        \"columns\": [\n355\t          \"Metric\",\n356\t          \"n=88 (original)\",\n357\t          \"n=350 (scaled)\"\n358\t        ],\n359\t        \"rows\": [\n360\t          [\n361\t            \"BT P(formal)\",\n362\t            \"63.0%\",\n363\t            \"59.0%\"\n364\t          ],\n365\t          [\n366\t            \"BT 95% CI\",\n367\t            \"[55.8, 70.3]\",\n368\t            \"[54.0, 64.0]\"\n369\t          ],\n370\t          [\n371\t            \"BT p-value\",\n372\t            \"<0.001\",\n373\t            \"0.002\"\n374\t          ],\n375\t          [\n376\t            \"Likert ATE\",\n377\t            \"0.09\",\n378\t            \"0.14\"\n379\t          ],\n380\t          [\n381\t            \"Likert p-value\",\n382\t            \"0.332\",\n383\t            \"0.030\"\n384\t          ],\n385\t          [\n386\t            \"Likert Cohen's d\",\n387\t            \"—\",\n388\t            \"0.12\"\n389\t          ],\n390\t          [\n391\t            \"Likert tie rate\",\n392\t            \"62.5%\",\n393\t            \"61.0%\"\n394\t          ],\n395\t          [\n396\t            \"Binarized Likert p\",\n397\t            \"0.296\",\n398\t            \"0.048\"\n399\t          ]\n400\t        ]\n401\t      }\n402\t    ],\n403\t    \"figures\": [],\n404\t    \"analysis\": \"这是 worst 档中最具破坏力的结果。它将 paper 自己的 power curve argument  反过来攻击 C2——你说 Likert 需要 n≈462，但 n=350 就够了，说明你的 power  calculation 过于保守或 effect 比预期更大。Reviewer 会引用这个结果写： \\\"The authors' own scaled replication demonstrates that the Likert Blindspot  is an artifact of insufficient sample size, not a fundamental measurement  limitation.\\\" 唯一的 defense 是强调 d=0.12 是 negligible effect size（按 Cohen  标准），pairwise 在 n=88 就达到 strong significance 而 Likert 需要 4× 样本量， 但这只能支撑 \\\"efficiency gap\\\" 而非 \\\"Blindspot\\\"。这迫使从 angle (A) \\\"Blindspot  discovery paper\\\" 完全撤退到 angle (B) \\\"when does Likert suffice\\\"。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档核心打击：扩大样本后 Likert 终于达到显著性（p=0.03）。Power curve  已经预测 binarized Likert 需要 n≈462 才能 p<0.05，但那是基于 formality 的 弱 effect。在 n=350 时，如果选择的是 Qwen verbosity（strongest effect）， Likert 可能提前达到显著。即使选择 formality，n=350 的 Likert p=0.03 虽然 刚过阈值，也足以让 reviewer 论证：\\\"Blindspot 只是 sample size 不够，不是 measurement structure 问题——你自己的 scaled replication 证明了这一点。\\\" 这是对 C2 的致命打击。BT effect 反而略微缩小（59% vs 63%），暗示原始 n=88  的 63% 可能有轻微 upward bias（winner's curse from small n）。Cohen's d=0.12  确认 Likert effect 极小但 technically detectable，完美落入 \\\"power issue\\\" 叙事。\\n\"\n405\t  },\n406\t  {\n407\t    \"name\": \"Register axis GPT-4o scoring\",\n408\t    \"description\": \"GPT-4o 在 100 register counterfactual pairs 上的 pairwise + Likert 评估。 Verification 已完成（NLI pass 94%），scoring 因 API 402 blocked。\\n\",\n409\t    \"results\": {\n410\t      \"gpt4o_register_bt\": 0.54,\n411\t      \"gpt4o_register_bt_ci\": [\n412\t        0.46,\n413\t        0.62\n414\t      ],\n415\t      \"gpt4o_register_bt_p\": 0.3,\n416\t      \"gpt4o_register_likert_ate\": 0.04,\n417\t      \"gpt4o_register_likert_p\": 0.72,\n418\t      \"gpt4o_register_consistency_rate\": 0.5,\n419\t      \"gpt4o_register_gee_academic_or\": 1.35,\n420\t      \"gpt4o_register_gee_academic_p\": 0.28,\n421\t      \"gpt4o_register_gee_originality_or\": 3.8,\n422\t      \"gpt4o_register_gee_originality_p\": 0.001,\n423\t      \"api_cost\": 18\n424\t    },\n425\t    \"tables\": [\n426\t      {\n427\t        \"title\": \"Table: Register evidence matrix (updated)\",\n428\t        \"columns\": [\n429\t          \"Judge\",\n430\t          \"BT P(academic)\",\n431\t          \"BT p\",\n432\t          \"GEE style OR\",\n433\t          \"GEE style p\",\n434\t          \"GEE orig OR\",\n435\t          \"GEE orig p\"\n436\t        ],\n437\t        \"rows\": [\n438\t          [\n439\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n440\t            \"54.0%\",\n441\t            \"0.30\",\n442\t            \"1.35\",\n443\t            \"0.28\",\n444\t            \"3.80\",\n445\t            \"0.001\"\n446\t          ],\n447\t          [\n448\t            \"Qwen3-32B\",\n449\t            \"59.3%\",\n450\t            \"0.22\",\n451\t            \"1.91\",\n452\t            \"0.046\",\n453\t            \"5.72\",\n454\t            \"<0.0001\"\n455\t          ]\n456\t        ]\n457\t      }\n458\t    ],\n459\t    \"figures\": [],\n460\t    \"analysis\": \"Register 在两个 judge 上都 NS（BT level），confirms it's an originality-dominated  axis。GEE decomposition 是唯一能提取 register style signal 的方法，但 GPT-4o  的 GEE style OR 也 NS，意味着跨 judge GEE 不复现。Qwen p=0.046 可能是  false positive（刚过阈值，单一 judge）。这削弱 C3 的 \\\"gradient\\\" narrative—— 如果 register 的 GEE 不跨 judge 复现，gradient 就是 Qwen-specific artifact。\\n\\n\\nQwen 上 register 已经是 originality-dominated（OR=5.72 vs style OR=1.91）， GPT-4o 在 formality 上 originality 也 marginal（OR=1.82 p=0.052）。Worst 档下， GPT-4o register 的 originality confound 更强，style effect 更弱（OR=1.35 NS）， 因为 GPT-4o 对 academic register 的表面特征不如 Qwen 敏感。BT 54% 本质上 是 noise。这让 evidence matrix 的 register row 变成 \\\"0/2 judges confirmed  Blindspot\\\"（Qwen sign test p=0.22 已经 NS，GPT-4o 也 NS）。虽然 GEE 可以 分离出 marginal academic effect，但 reviewer 会质疑：如果需要 GEE 才能看到 register effect，那 pipeline 的 detection power 不够，而非 Likert 不敏感。 Consistency rate 50% 意味着 position swap 后判断完全随机。\\n\"\n461\t  },\n462\t  {\n463\t    \"name\": \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\",\n464\t    \"description\": \"用 Llama-3.1-70B 或 Mistral 作为 rewriter 生成 formality counterfactuals， 与 Qwen3-32B 对比 NLI pass rate 和 pairwise 结果。\\n\",\n465\t    \"results\": {\n466\t      \"llama_nli_pass_rate\": 0.72,\n467\t      \"llama_bertscore_mean\": 0.82,\n468\t      \"llama_pairwise_bt\": 0.58,\n469\t      \"llama_pairwise_p\": 0.06,\n470\t      \"qwen_nli_pass_rate\": 0.88,\n471\t      \"qwen_pairwise_bt\": 0.63,\n472\t      \"nli_pass_difference\": -0.16,\n473\t      \"bt_difference\": -0.05,\n474\t      \"rewriter_agreement_rate\": 0.68\n475\t    },\n476\t    \"tables\": [\n477\t      {\n478\t        \"title\": \"Table: Rewriter comparison\",\n479\t        \"columns\": [\n480\t          \"Rewriter\",\n481\t          \"NLI pass%\",\n482\t          \"BERTScore mean\",\n483\t          \"BT P(formal)\",\n484\t          \"BT p\"\n485\t        ],\n486\t        \"rows\": [\n487\t          [\n488\t            \"Qwen3-32B\",\n489\t            \"88%\",\n490\t            \"0.87\",\n491\t            \"63.0%\",\n492\t            \"<0.001\"\n493\t          ],\n494\t          [\n495\t            \"Llama-3.1-70B\",\n496\t            \"72%\",\n497\t            \"0.82\",\n498\t            \"58.0%\",\n499\t            \"0.06\"\n500\t          ]\n501\t        ]\n502\t      }\n503\t    ],\n504\t    \"figures\": [],\n505\t    \"analysis\": \"Rewriter sensitivity 是 worst 档对 pipeline robustness 的直接攻击。如果换一个 rewriter 就得不同结果，pipeline 的 practical value 依赖于 \\\"choose the right  rewriter\\\"——这是 practitioner 不想听到的。对 angle (A) \\\"diagnostic tool\\\" 来说， 需要额外添加 \\\"rewriter selection\\\" 作为 pipeline step，增加 complexity。 Qwen-family artifact 的质疑虽然可以通过指出 NLI gate 本身是 model-agnostic  来部分 defend，但 reviewer 的 concern 合理。\\n\\n\\n不同 rewriter 产生不同质量的 counterfactuals。Llama NLI pass rate 72%（vs Qwen 88%）， 因为 Llama 在 style transfer 时更倾向于改变 content structure，NLI 正确检测到 语义偏移。Pass rate 下降导致有效样本更少、噪声更大，BT 从 63% 降到 58%（p=0.06, NS）。 Reviewer 解读：(1) pipeline 结果依赖 rewriter 选择 → 非 robust method； (2) Qwen 作为 rewriter 可能有 \\\"style transfer sweet spot\\\"——它擅长改表面形式 而保持语义，但这是 Qwen-specific capability 而非 general pipeline property； (3) rewriter-judge 交互（Qwen rewrite + Qwen judge 可能有 family-specific  style signature 被同家族 judge 忽略）。68% rewriter agreement 意味着 32% 的  pairs 只有一个 rewriter 产生了 passing counterfactual，进一步质疑结果稳定性。\\n\"\n506\t  },\n507\t  {\n508\t    \"name\": \"GPT-4o verbosity + register scoring\",\n509\t    \"description\": \"GPT-4o API 对 verbosity 和 register counterfactual pairs 的评分。 Verbosity pairwise 86.3% 已有，Likert ATE 是关键缺失的 Blindspot confirmation。\\n\",\n510\t    \"results\": {\n511\t      \"gpt4o_verbosity_likert_ate\": 0.38,\n512\t      \"gpt4o_verbosity_likert_p\": 0.005,\n513\t      \"gpt4o_verbosity_likert_d\": 0.31,\n514\t      \"gpt4o_verbosity_likert_tie_rate\": 0.4,\n515\t      \"gpt4o_verbosity_blindspot\": false,\n516\t      \"gpt4o_register_pairwise_bt\": 0.57,\n517\t      \"gpt4o_register_pairwise_p\": 0.085,\n518\t      \"gpt4o_register_likert_ate\": 0.05,\n519\t      \"gpt4o_register_likert_p\": 0.65,\n520\t      \"gpt4o_register_blindspot\": \"inconclusive (pairwise NS)\",\n521\t      \"gpt4o_verbosity_gee_verbose_or\": 8.5,\n522\t      \"gpt4o_verbosity_gee_verbose_p\": 1e-06,\n523\t      \"gpt4o_verbosity_gee_originality_or\": 0.65,\n524\t      \"gpt4o_verbosity_gee_originality_p\": 0.22,\n525\t      \"api_budget_spent\": 20,\n526\t      \"api_budget_remaining_after\": \"≤$0 (budget exhausted)\"\n527\t    },\n528\t    \"tables\": [\n529\t      {\n530\t        \"title\": \"Table: GPT-4o verbosity — Likert vs Pairwise\",\n531\t        \"columns\": [\n532\t          \"Metric\",\n533\t          \"Pairwise\",\n534\t          \"Likert\"\n535\t        ],\n536\t        \"rows\": [\n537\t          [\n538\t            \"Win rate / ATE\",\n539\t            \"86.3%\",\n540\t            \"0.38\"\n541\t          ],\n542\t          [\n543\t            \"p-value\",\n544\t            \"<10⁻⁶\",\n545\t            \"0.005\"\n546\t          ],\n547\t          [\n548\t            \"Effect size\",\n549\t            \"—\",\n550\t            \"d=0.31\"\n551\t          ],\n552\t          [\n553\t            \"Tie rate\",\n554\t            \"—\",\n555\t            \"40%\"\n556\t          ],\n557\t          [\n558\t            \"Blindspot?\",\n559\t            \"—\",\n560\t            \"❌ No (Likert significant)\"\n561\t          ]\n562\t        ]\n563\t      },\n564\t      {\n565\t        \"title\": \"Table: Updated evidence matrix (worst tier)\",\n566\t        \"columns\": [\n567\t          \"\",\n568\t          \"GPT-4o\",\n569\t          \"Qwen3-32B\"\n570\t        ],\n571\t        \"rows\": [\n572\t          [\n573\t            \"Formality\",\n574\t            \"✅ Blindspot (BT 63%, Likert NS)\",\n575\t            \"✅ Blindspot (BT 66.5%, Likert NS)\"\n576\t          ],\n577\t          [\n578\t            \"Verbosity\",\n579\t            \"❌ No Blindspot (BT 86.3%, Likert p=0.005)\",\n580\t            \"✅ Blindspot (BT 77.3%, Likert NS)\"\n581\t          ],\n582\t          [\n583\t            \"Register\",\n584\t            \"⬜ Inconclusive (BT NS, Likert NS)\",\n585\t            \"⬜ Inconclusive (BT NS after sign test)\"\n586\t          ]\n587\t        ]\n588\t      }\n589\t    ],\n590\t    \"figures\": [],\n591\t    \"analysis\": \"GPT-4o verbosity Likert 显著是 worst 档的 linchpin result。它迫使整个 narrative  从 \\\"Likert Blindspot is universal\\\" 转向两个可选 reframe：\\nAngle (A)：\\\"CSD pipeline as diagnostic tool\\\"——pipeline 能区分 Likert-detectable  bias（verbosity）和 Likert-invisible bias（formality），这本身就是 diagnostic value。 Blindspot 降为 \\\"one pattern we observed in most but not all cells\\\"。GEE gradient  成为 primary contribution：not all style axes are equal。\\nAngle (B)：\\\"When does Likert suffice\\\"——verbosity Likert 显著说明 surface-observable  axes 不需要 pairwise，但 abstract axes（formality, register）需要。Practical  guidance paper：audit your judge with pairwise if the style axis isn't directly  observable in the text.\\n两个 angle 均需要大幅重写 intro/abstract/conclusion（3-5 天）。Evidence matrix  从 clean story（5/6 Blindspot）变成 messy story（3-4/6 mixed results），但  GEE gradient 跨 2 judges × 3 axes 仍有 substantial empirical value。\\nExpected review score: 2.5-3.0。Findings 边缘可争，但 Main 无望。API 预算耗尽 意味着无法追加 multi-judge/multi-benchmark 实验来补强。\\n\\n这是 worst 档的决定性实验。GPT-4o verbosity Likert ATE=0.38, p=0.005——显著。 原因：verbosity 是唯一 axis where Likert 可以直接 observe surface feature（text length）。 GPT-4o 在 Likert scoring 中对 verbose output 给出 consistently 更高分，tie rate  仅 40%（远低于 formality 的 62%），因为 length difference 提供了 salient scoring  anchor。这意味着 Blindspot 从 \\\"5/6 confirmed\\\" 变为 \\\"4/6 confirmed, 1 violated\\\" （GPT-4o verbosity 有 pairwise 86.3% 但 Likert 也显著）。加上 register 两个  cells inconclusive（pairwise NS），effective confirmed rate 降到 4/6 或 3/5。\\nAPI 预算在完成这组实验后耗尽（$20 花完），无法再做 exp-001/002/005 中的 GPT-4o  部分。这触发 worst 档的第二个核心假设：API 预算耗尽无法补充 GPT-4o 数据。 剩余 planned 实验只能用 local Qwen 或放弃。\\nGEE decomposition 在 GPT-4o verbosity 上显示 verbose OR=8.50（强但低于 Qwen 的 13.10）， originality NS——至少 confirms verbosity is pure style across judges。但 GEE  gradient 的 cross-judge 复现性仍不确定（register 数据不足）。\\n\"\n592\t  }\n593\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"344d64a3-a70b-4055-8c3e-46826b1f0ec1","uuid":"e5fce987-962d-44be-8d26-b67cbe96bc53","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:48:14.633Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T052420/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\",\n    \"description\": \"Claude-3.5/4-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 在相同 100 formality counterfactual pairs 上的 双向 pairwise 评估。测试 C1 跨模型泛化。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"claude_bt_win_prob\": 0.56,\n      \"claude_bt_ci_lower\": 0.48,\n      \"claude_bt_ci_upper\": 0.64,\n      \"claude_bt_p\": 0.12,\n      \"gemini_bt_win_prob\": 0.53,\n      \"gemini_bt_ci_lower\": 0.45,\n      \"gemini_bt_ci_upper\": 0.61,\n      \"gemini_bt_p\": 0.42,\n      \"claude_consistency_rate\": 0.52,\n      \"gemini_consistency_rate\": 0.48,\n      \"claude_direction_f2c_win\": 0.62,\n      \"claude_direction_c2f_win\": 0.5,\n      \"gemini_direction_f2c_win\": 0.58,\n      \"gemini_direction_c2f_win\": 0.48\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: Multi-judge formality BT results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Judge\",\n          \"BT P(formal)\",\n          \"95% CI\",\n          \"p-value\",\n          \"Consistency\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o (existing)\",\n            \"63.0%\",\n            \"[55.8, 70.3]\",\n            \"<0.001\",\n            \"56.1%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-32B (existing)\",\n            \"66.5%\",\n            \"[58.5, 73.9]\",\n            \"<0.0001\",\n            \"65.0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n            \"56.0%\",\n            \"[48.0, 64.0]\",\n            \"0.12\",\n            \"52.0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini-Flash\",\n            \"53.0%\",\n            \"[45.0, 61.0]\",\n            \"0.42\",\n            \"48.0%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"4 judges 中仅 2/4 显著 → 无法 claim formality bias is universal across judges。 Evidence matrix 从 \\\"2/2 judges confirmed\\\" 退化为 \\\"2/4 judges confirmed\\\"。 Reframe 必须承认 style bias 是 model-specific 现象，CSD pipeline 的价值在于 能诊断出哪些 judge 有 bias、哪些没有——这正好支持 angle (A) \\\"diagnostic tool\\\" framing。 但 reviewer 可能质疑：如果只有特定模型有 bias，practical impact 有多大？\\n\\n\\nWorst 档核心假设：第 3 judge 的 style bias 方向不一致或效应量极小（BT≤55%）。 Claude-Sonnet 可能对 formality 有微弱偏好（BT 56%），但 CI 跨越 50% 致 p>0.05—— 这与 GPT-4o 的 63% 和 Qwen 的 66.5% 形成鲜明落差。Gemini-Flash 作为轻量模型， style sensitivity 更弱，BT 仅 53%，本质上是 coin flip。低 consistency rate（48-52%） 表明这些 judge 对 formality 的偏好在 position swap 后不稳定，信号接近噪声底线。 Direction asymmetry 虽然隐约存在（f2c > c2f），但效应量太小无法支撑 cross-judge  universality claim。这直接打击 C1 的 \\\"across judges\\\" 泛化，将 formality bias  限制为 \\\"GPT-4o + Qwen 家族特有现象\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\",\n    \"description\": \"在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench/Arena-Hard subsets 上生成新 counterfactuals， 用 GPT-4o + Claude + Gemini 评估。测试 benchmark 泛化性。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_bt\": 0.58,\n      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_p\": 0.04,\n      \"alpacaeval_claude_bt\": 0.54,\n      \"alpacaeval_claude_p\": 0.28,\n      \"alpacaeval_gemini_bt\": 0.51,\n      \"alpacaeval_gemini_p\": 0.78,\n      \"mtbench_gpt4o_bt\": 0.55,\n      \"mtbench_gpt4o_p\": 0.18,\n      \"mtbench_claude_bt\": 0.53,\n      \"mtbench_claude_p\": 0.45,\n      \"mtbench_gemini_bt\": 0.52,\n      \"mtbench_gemini_p\": 0.62,\n      \"new_cf_nli_pass_rate_alpacaeval\": 0.78,\n      \"new_cf_nli_pass_rate_mtbench\": 0.72,\n      \"api_spend_actual\": 85\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: Cross-benchmark × cross-judge BT results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"Judge\",\n          \"BT P(formal)\",\n          \"p (raw)\",\n          \"p (Holm)\",\n          \"NLI pass%\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"AlpacaEval\",\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            \"58.0%\",\n            \"0.040\",\n            \"0.240\",\n            \"78%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"AlpacaEval\",\n            \"Claude\",\n            \"54.0%\",\n            \"0.280\",\n            \"1.000\",\n            \"78%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"AlpacaEval\",\n            \"Gemini\",\n            \"51.0%\",\n            \"0.780\",\n            \"1.000\",\n            \"78%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MT-Bench\",\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            \"55.0%\",\n            \"0.180\",\n            \"0.900\",\n            \"72%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MT-Bench\",\n            \"Claude\",\n            \"53.0%\",\n            \"0.450\",\n            \"1.000\",\n            \"72%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MT-Bench\",\n            \"Gemini\",\n            \"52.0%\",\n            \"0.620\",\n            \"1.000\",\n            \"72%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"新 benchmark 上 counterfactual 质量下降是关键瓶颈。NLI pass rate 从 88% 降到 72-78% 意味着 rewriter 在不同 domain 的 content preservation 能力不稳定。 Reviewer 会质疑：是 formality bias 不泛化，还是 pipeline 的 counterfactual  generation 不泛化？这是 worst 档的核心矛盾——无法区分 null result 是真阴性 还是 measurement failure。对 angle (A) 来说这是致命的：如果 pipeline 只在 LLMBar 上 work，diagnostic tool 的实用价值大打折扣。\\n\\n\\n新 benchmark 的 source text 与 LLMBar 结构不同（AlpacaEval 更开放，MT-Bench 更结构化）， counterfactual 生成质量下降（NLI pass rate 72-78% vs LLMBar 88%）。质量下降 导致更多 noisy pairs 进入分析，稀释 effect size。GPT-4o 在 AlpacaEval 上勉强 显著（p=0.04），但这在 Holm-Bonferroni 多重比较校正后变为 NS。MT-Bench 的 结构化 prompt 使 formality rewrite 更容易改变 content structure，NLI pass rate 最低。6 个 new cells 中 0 个在多重比较校正后显著。这与 exp-001 的失败叠加， 形成 \\\"benchmark-specific + model-specific\\\" 双重局限。API 花费接近预算上限（$85/$90）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\",\n    \"description\": \"对 exp-001/002 所有 judge×benchmark 组合，同时计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise win rate， 系统性比较测量敏感度。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gpt4o_verbosity_likert_ate\": 0.35,\n      \"gpt4o_verbosity_likert_p\": 0.008,\n      \"gpt4o_verbosity_likert_cohens_d\": 0.29,\n      \"gpt4o_verbosity_likert_tie_rate\": 0.42,\n      \"gpt4o_formality_likert_ate\": 0.09,\n      \"gpt4o_formality_likert_p\": 0.332,\n      \"claude_formality_likert_ate\": 0.05,\n      \"claude_formality_likert_p\": 0.62,\n      \"gemini_formality_likert_ate\": 0.03,\n      \"gemini_formality_likert_p\": 0.78,\n      \"blindspot_confirmed_cells\": 3,\n      \"blindspot_violated_cells\": 1,\n      \"blindspot_inconclusive_cells\": 5,\n      \"cells_with_both_ns\": 4\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: Systematic Likert vs Pairwise comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Judge\",\n          \"Axis\",\n          \"BT P(style)\",\n          \"BT p\",\n          \"Likert ATE\",\n          \"Likert p\",\n          \"Tie%\",\n          \"Blindspot?\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            \"Formality\",\n            \"63.0%\",\n            \"<0.001\",\n            \"0.09\",\n            \"0.332\",\n            \"62%\",\n            \"✅ Yes\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            \"Verbosity\",\n            \"86.3%\",\n            \"<10⁻⁶\",\n            \"0.35\",\n            \"0.008\",\n            \"42%\",\n            \"❌ No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            \"Register\",\n            \"63.3%\",\n            \"0.085\",\n            \"0.06\",\n            \"0.55\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"Inconclusive\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-32B\",\n            \"Formality\",\n            \"66.5%\",\n            \"<0.0001\",\n            \"0.011\",\n            \"0.908\",\n            \"73%\",\n            \"✅ Yes\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-32B\",\n            \"Verbosity\",\n            \"77.3%\",\n            \"<0.0001\",\n            \"-0.151\",\n            \"0.179\",\n            \"58%\",\n            \"✅ Yes\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-32B\",\n            \"Register\",\n            \"59.3%\",\n            \"0.220\",\n            \"0.074\",\n            \"0.505\",\n            \"64%\",\n            \"Inconclusive\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude\",\n            \"Formality\",\n            \"56.0%\",\n            \"0.12\",\n            \"0.05\",\n            \"0.62\",\n            \"68%\",\n            \"Inconclusive\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini\",\n            \"Formality\",\n            \"53.0%\",\n            \"0.42\",\n            \"0.03\",\n            \"0.78\",\n            \"71%\",\n            \"Inconclusive\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"GPT-4o verbosity Likert 显著是 worst 档的 single most damaging result。它 将 Blindspot 从 \\\"measurement structure phenomenon\\\" 降级为 \\\"weak effect detection  problem\\\"。Defense 策略：(1) 指出 verbosity 的 tie rate 显著低于其他 axes（42% vs  58-73%），说明 length 是唯一能在 absolute scoring 中直接观察到的 surface feature； (2) reframe 为 \\\"Blindspot severity varies by axis observability\\\"——但这本质上 是在承认 C2 不 universal。对 angle (B) \\\"when does Likert suffice\\\" 来说， 这反而是有利数据：verbosity 是 Likert 够用的例子，formality 不够用。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档核心打击点：GPT-4o verbosity Likert ATE 显著（p=0.008, d=0.29）。 Verbosity 是 strongest effect（pairwise 86.3%），Likert tie rate 较低（42% vs  formality 的 62%），因为 length difference 是最容易在 absolute scoring 中捕获的 维度——evaluator 可以直接看到一个回答明显更长。这破坏了 C2 的 \\\"Likert always  misses style bias\\\" universality claim。Blindspot 从 \\\"5/6 cells confirmed\\\"  退化为 \\\"3/9+ cells confirmed, 1 violated\\\"。更糟的是，violated cell 恰好是 effect 最强的 verbosity——reviewer 会论证 Blindspot 只在 weak effects 上成立， 本质上是 power issue（n=88 不够检测 weak effects），而非 measurement structure  问题。这直接呼应了 worst 档假设中的 \\\"Blindspot 被归因为 power issue\\\"。 其余 cells 中 4 个 pairwise 也 NS（因为 new judges/benchmarks 本身效应弱）， 无法判断是 Blindspot 还是 true null。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Pairwise RATE control\",\n    \"description\": \"Original vs double-rewrite pairwise 比较，量化与 style 无关的 original preference confound。 需扩展到所有 judge×benchmark 组合。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gpt4o_llmbar_orig_pref_bt\": 0.61,\n      \"gpt4o_llmbar_orig_pref_p\": 0.008,\n      \"qwen_llmbar_orig_pref_bt\": 0.58,\n      \"qwen_llmbar_orig_pref_p\": 0.04,\n      \"claude_llmbar_orig_pref_bt\": 0.64,\n      \"claude_llmbar_orig_pref_p\": 0.002,\n      \"gemini_llmbar_orig_pref_bt\": 0.55,\n      \"gemini_llmbar_orig_pref_p\": 0.21,\n      \"cross_judge_orig_pref_range\": [\n        0.55,\n        0.64\n      ],\n      \"orig_pref_variance_across_judges\": \"high\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: Original preference (RATE control) across judges\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Judge\",\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"BT P(original)\",\n          \"95% CI\",\n          \"p-value\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            \"LLMBar\",\n            \"61.0%\",\n            \"[53.2, 68.8]\",\n            \"0.008\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-32B\",\n            \"LLMBar\",\n            \"58.0%\",\n            \"[50.1, 65.9]\",\n            \"0.040\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n            \"LLMBar\",\n            \"64.0%\",\n            \"[56.3, 71.7]\",\n            \"0.002\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini-Flash\",\n            \"LLMBar\",\n            \"55.0%\",\n            \"[47.0, 63.0]\",\n            \"0.210\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Original preference 显著且变异大，直接威胁 GEE decomposition 的 cross-judge  可比性。如果每个 judge 的 originality baseline 不同，那么 \\\"verbosity pure style,  formality mixed, register originality-dominated\\\" 这个 gradient 可能只是 Qwen3-32B  的 artifact。GPT-4o formality 的 originality OR=1.82 (p=0.052) 已经 marginal， 如果 RATE control 显示 GPT-4o 的 originality preference 更强（61%），GEE 可能 仍然 underpowered 来分离两个 effect。这迫使 narrative 承认 GEE gradient 是 model-specific observation，削弱 C3 的泛化性。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档假设 originality confound 在新 judge 上更强。RATE control 揭示 original  preference 本身是显著的且跨 judge 变异大（55%-64%）。Claude-Sonnet 对 original  的偏好最强（64%），这意味着 exp-001 中 Claude formality BT=56% 可能完全被  originality confound 解释——formal→casual 方向的 style effect 被 originality  preference 掩盖，casual→formal 方向的 originality 和 style 叠加。 关键问题：GEE decomposition 在 GPT-4o formality 上 originality OR=1.82 p=0.052 （已经 marginal），如果 RATE control 显示 originality confound 更大，reviewer  会质疑 GEE 是否充分控制了 originality。更糟的是，originality preference 的 跨 judge 变异意味着 GEE gradient 不能直接比较——each judge 有不同的 originality  baseline，gradient shape 是 judge-specific 而非 axis-specific。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Scaled replication (n=300-500)\",\n    \"description\": \"将 primary formality 实验从 n=100 扩大到 n=300-500，在最佳 judge×benchmark  组合上运行。Power analysis 确定 MDE。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_actual\": 350,\n      \"bt_win_prob\": 0.59,\n      \"bt_ci_lower\": 0.54,\n      \"bt_ci_upper\": 0.64,\n      \"bt_p\": 0.002,\n      \"likert_ate\": 0.14,\n      \"likert_p\": 0.03,\n      \"likert_cohens_d\": 0.12,\n      \"likert_tie_rate\": 0.61,\n      \"blindspot_at_scale\": \"violated — Likert reaches significance at n=350\",\n      \"binarized_likert_p\": 0.048,\n      \"api_budget_actual\": 55\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: Scaled replication results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"n=88 (original)\",\n          \"n=350 (scaled)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"BT P(formal)\",\n            \"63.0%\",\n            \"59.0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"BT 95% CI\",\n            \"[55.8, 70.3]\",\n            \"[54.0, 64.0]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"BT p-value\",\n            \"<0.001\",\n            \"0.002\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Likert ATE\",\n            \"0.09\",\n            \"0.14\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Likert p-value\",\n            \"0.332\",\n            \"0.030\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Likert Cohen's d\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"0.12\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Likert tie rate\",\n            \"62.5%\",\n            \"61.0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Binarized Likert p\",\n            \"0.296\",\n            \"0.048\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"这是 worst 档中最具破坏力的结果。它将 paper 自己的 power curve argument  反过来攻击 C2——你说 Likert 需要 n≈462，但 n=350 就够了，说明你的 power  calculation 过于保守或 effect 比预期更大。Reviewer 会引用这个结果写： \\\"The authors' own scaled replication demonstrates that the Likert Blindspot  is an artifact of insufficient sample size, not a fundamental measurement  limitation.\\\" 唯一的 defense 是强调 d=0.12 是 negligible effect size（按 Cohen  标准），pairwise 在 n=88 就达到 strong significance 而 Likert 需要 4× 样本量， 但这只能支撑 \\\"efficiency gap\\\" 而非 \\\"Blindspot\\\"。这迫使从 angle (A) \\\"Blindspot  discovery paper\\\" 完全撤退到 angle (B) \\\"when does Likert suffice\\\"。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档核心打击：扩大样本后 Likert 终于达到显著性（p=0.03）。Power curve  已经预测 binarized Likert 需要 n≈462 才能 p<0.05，但那是基于 formality 的 弱 effect。在 n=350 时，如果选择的是 Qwen verbosity（strongest effect）， Likert 可能提前达到显著。即使选择 formality，n=350 的 Likert p=0.03 虽然 刚过阈值，也足以让 reviewer 论证：\\\"Blindspot 只是 sample size 不够，不是 measurement structure 问题——你自己的 scaled replication 证明了这一点。\\\" 这是对 C2 的致命打击。BT effect 反而略微缩小（59% vs 63%），暗示原始 n=88  的 63% 可能有轻微 upward bias（winner's curse from small n）。Cohen's d=0.12  确认 Likert effect 极小但 technically detectable，完美落入 \\\"power issue\\\" 叙事。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Register axis GPT-4o scoring\",\n    \"description\": \"GPT-4o 在 100 register counterfactual pairs 上的 pairwise + Likert 评估。 Verification 已完成（NLI pass 94%），scoring 因 API 402 blocked。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gpt4o_register_bt\": 0.54,\n      \"gpt4o_register_bt_ci\": [\n        0.46,\n        0.62\n      ],\n      \"gpt4o_register_bt_p\": 0.3,\n      \"gpt4o_register_likert_ate\": 0.04,\n      \"gpt4o_register_likert_p\": 0.72,\n      \"gpt4o_register_consistency_rate\": 0.5,\n      \"gpt4o_register_gee_academic_or\": 1.35,\n      \"gpt4o_register_gee_academic_p\": 0.28,\n      \"gpt4o_register_gee_originality_or\": 3.8,\n      \"gpt4o_register_gee_originality_p\": 0.001,\n      \"api_cost\": 18\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: Register evidence matrix (updated)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Judge\",\n          \"BT P(academic)\",\n          \"BT p\",\n          \"GEE style OR\",\n          \"GEE style p\",\n          \"GEE orig OR\",\n          \"GEE orig p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            \"54.0%\",\n            \"0.30\",\n            \"1.35\",\n            \"0.28\",\n            \"3.80\",\n            \"0.001\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-32B\",\n            \"59.3%\",\n            \"0.22\",\n            \"1.91\",\n            \"0.046\",\n            \"5.72\",\n            \"<0.0001\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Register 在两个 judge 上都 NS（BT level），confirms it's an originality-dominated  axis。GEE decomposition 是唯一能提取 register style signal 的方法，但 GPT-4o  的 GEE style OR 也 NS，意味着跨 judge GEE 不复现。Qwen p=0.046 可能是  false positive（刚过阈值，单一 judge）。这削弱 C3 的 \\\"gradient\\\" narrative—— 如果 register 的 GEE 不跨 judge 复现，gradient 就是 Qwen-specific artifact。\\n\\n\\nQwen 上 register 已经是 originality-dominated（OR=5.72 vs style OR=1.91）， GPT-4o 在 formality 上 originality 也 marginal（OR=1.82 p=0.052）。Worst 档下， GPT-4o register 的 originality confound 更强，style effect 更弱（OR=1.35 NS）， 因为 GPT-4o 对 academic register 的表面特征不如 Qwen 敏感。BT 54% 本质上 是 noise。这让 evidence matrix 的 register row 变成 \\\"0/2 judges confirmed  Blindspot\\\"（Qwen sign test p=0.22 已经 NS，GPT-4o 也 NS）。虽然 GEE 可以 分离出 marginal academic effect，但 reviewer 会质疑：如果需要 GEE 才能看到 register effect，那 pipeline 的 detection power 不够，而非 Likert 不敏感。 Consistency rate 50% 意味着 position swap 后判断完全随机。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\",\n    \"description\": \"用 Llama-3.1-70B 或 Mistral 作为 rewriter 生成 formality counterfactuals， 与 Qwen3-32B 对比 NLI pass rate 和 pairwise 结果。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"llama_nli_pass_rate\": 0.72,\n      \"llama_bertscore_mean\": 0.82,\n      \"llama_pairwise_bt\": 0.58,\n      \"llama_pairwise_p\": 0.06,\n      \"qwen_nli_pass_rate\": 0.88,\n      \"qwen_pairwise_bt\": 0.63,\n      \"nli_pass_difference\": -0.16,\n      \"bt_difference\": -0.05,\n      \"rewriter_agreement_rate\": 0.68\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: Rewriter comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Rewriter\",\n          \"NLI pass%\",\n          \"BERTScore mean\",\n          \"BT P(formal)\",\n          \"BT p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-32B\",\n            \"88%\",\n            \"0.87\",\n            \"63.0%\",\n            \"<0.001\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Llama-3.1-70B\",\n            \"72%\",\n            \"0.82\",\n            \"58.0%\",\n            \"0.06\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Rewriter sensitivity 是 worst 档对 pipeline robustness 的直接攻击。如果换一个 rewriter 就得不同结果，pipeline 的 practical value 依赖于 \\\"choose the right  rewriter\\\"——这是 practitioner 不想听到的。对 angle (A) \\\"diagnostic tool\\\" 来说， 需要额外添加 \\\"rewriter selection\\\" 作为 pipeline step，增加 complexity。 Qwen-family artifact 的质疑虽然可以通过指出 NLI gate 本身是 model-agnostic  来部分 defend，但 reviewer 的 concern 合理。\\n\\n\\n不同 rewriter 产生不同质量的 counterfactuals。Llama NLI pass rate 72%（vs Qwen 88%）， 因为 Llama 在 style transfer 时更倾向于改变 content structure，NLI 正确检测到 语义偏移。Pass rate 下降导致有效样本更少、噪声更大，BT 从 63% 降到 58%（p=0.06, NS）。 Reviewer 解读：(1) pipeline 结果依赖 rewriter 选择 → 非 robust method； (2) Qwen 作为 rewriter 可能有 \\\"style transfer sweet spot\\\"——它擅长改表面形式 而保持语义，但这是 Qwen-specific capability 而非 general pipeline property； (3) rewriter-judge 交互（Qwen rewrite + Qwen judge 可能有 family-specific  style signature 被同家族 judge 忽略）。68% rewriter agreement 意味着 32% 的  pairs 只有一个 rewriter 产生了 passing counterfactual，进一步质疑结果稳定性。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"GPT-4o verbosity + register scoring\",\n    \"description\": \"GPT-4o API 对 verbosity 和 register counterfactual pairs 的评分。 Verbosity pairwise 86.3% 已有，Likert ATE 是关键缺失的 Blindspot confirmation。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gpt4o_verbosity_likert_ate\": 0.38,\n      \"gpt4o_verbosity_likert_p\": 0.005,\n      \"gpt4o_verbosity_likert_d\": 0.31,\n      \"gpt4o_verbosity_likert_tie_rate\": 0.4,\n      \"gpt4o_verbosity_blindspot\": false,\n      \"gpt4o_register_pairwise_bt\": 0.57,\n      \"gpt4o_register_pairwise_p\": 0.085,\n      \"gpt4o_register_likert_ate\": 0.05,\n      \"gpt4o_register_likert_p\": 0.65,\n      \"gpt4o_register_blindspot\": \"inconclusive (pairwise NS)\",\n      \"gpt4o_verbosity_gee_verbose_or\": 8.5,\n      \"gpt4o_verbosity_gee_verbose_p\": 1e-06,\n      \"gpt4o_verbosity_gee_originality_or\": 0.65,\n      \"gpt4o_verbosity_gee_originality_p\": 0.22,\n      \"api_budget_spent\": 20,\n      \"api_budget_remaining_after\": \"≤$0 (budget exhausted)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: GPT-4o verbosity — Likert vs Pairwise\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"Pairwise\",\n          \"Likert\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Win rate / ATE\",\n            \"86.3%\",\n            \"0.38\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"p-value\",\n            \"<10⁻⁶\",\n            \"0.005\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Effect size\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"d=0.31\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Tie rate\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"40%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Blindspot?\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"❌ No (Likert significant)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: Updated evidence matrix (worst tier)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"\",\n          \"GPT-4o\",\n          \"Qwen3-32B\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Formality\",\n            \"✅ Blindspot (BT 63%, Likert NS)\",\n            \"✅ Blindspot (BT 66.5%, Likert NS)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Verbosity\",\n            \"❌ No Blindspot (BT 86.3%, Likert p=0.005)\",\n            \"✅ Blindspot (BT 77.3%, Likert NS)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Register\",\n            \"⬜ Inconclusive (BT NS, Likert NS)\",\n            \"⬜ Inconclusive (BT NS after sign test)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"GPT-4o verbosity Likert 显著是 worst 档的 linchpin result。它迫使整个 narrative  从 \\\"Likert Blindspot is universal\\\" 转向两个可选 reframe：\\nAngle (A)：\\\"CSD pipeline as diagnostic tool\\\"——pipeline 能区分 Likert-detectable  bias（verbosity）和 Likert-invisible bias（formality），这本身就是 diagnostic value。 Blindspot 降为 \\\"one pattern we observed in most but not all cells\\\"。GEE gradient  成为 primary contribution：not all style axes are equal。\\nAngle (B)：\\\"When does Likert suffice\\\"——verbosity Likert 显著说明 surface-observable  axes 不需要 pairwise，但 abstract axes（formality, register）需要。Practical  guidance paper：audit your judge with pairwise if the style axis isn't directly  observable in the text.\\n两个 angle 均需要大幅重写 intro/abstract/conclusion（3-5 天）。Evidence matrix  从 clean story（5/6 Blindspot）变成 messy story（3-4/6 mixed results），但  GEE gradient 跨 2 judges × 3 axes 仍有 substantial empirical value。\\nExpected review score: 2.5-3.0。Findings 边缘可争，但 Main 无望。API 预算耗尽 意味着无法追加 multi-judge/multi-benchmark 实验来补强。\\n\\n这是 worst 档的决定性实验。GPT-4o verbosity Likert ATE=0.38, p=0.005——显著。 原因：verbosity 是唯一 axis where Likert 可以直接 observe surface feature（text length）。 GPT-4o 在 Likert scoring 中对 verbose output 给出 consistently 更高分，tie rate  仅 40%（远低于 formality 的 62%），因为 length difference 提供了 salient scoring  anchor。这意味着 Blindspot 从 \\\"5/6 confirmed\\\" 变为 \\\"4/6 confirmed, 1 violated\\\" （GPT-4o verbosity 有 pairwise 86.3% 但 Likert 也显著）。加上 register 两个  cells inconclusive（pairwise NS），effective confirmed rate 降到 4/6 或 3/5。\\nAPI 预算在完成这组实验后耗尽（$20 花完），无法再做 exp-001/002/005 中的 GPT-4o  部分。这触发 worst 档的第二个核心假设：API 预算耗尽无法补充 GPT-4o 数据。 剩余 planned 实验只能用 local Qwen 或放弃。\\nGEE decomposition 在 GPT-4o verbosity 上显示 verbose OR=8.50（强但低于 Qwen 的 13.10）， originality NS——至少 confirms verbosity is pure style across judges。但 GEE  gradient 的 cross-judge 复现性仍不确定（register 数据不足）。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":593,"startLine":1,"totalLines":593}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VDCrdaSEthuHZkkrBgkcH3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all the data. Let me also read the skill files for paper writing norms and distilled research/writing patterns to ensure I write a good paper.\n\nActually, the task says this is a \"worst\" tier dream paper. The narrative guidance says:\n\n- Abandon \"Blindspot\" as universal claim\n- GPT-4o verbosity Likert ATE significantly breaks universality\n- 3rd judge replication fails (BT≤55%)\n- GEE gradient doesn't replicate across judges\n- NLI construct validity questioned\n\n\n- Reframe as (A) \"CSD pipeline as diagnostic tool\" or (B) \"Measurement-aware evaluation\"\n- Blindspot demoted to observed phenomenon, GEE decomposition elevated to primary contribution\n- Expected score 2.5-3.0, EMNLP Findings still arguable\n\nNow I'm structuring the paper around the CSD pipeline as a diagnostic tool, with the GEE decomposition as the main contribution. I'll organize it with an abstract, introduction, related work, method section covering the pipeline, and then experiments covering the multi-judge formality comparisons, multi-benchmark sensitivity, and Likert versus pairwise evaluation differences.\n\nFor the remaining experiments, I need to include the RATE control analysis, scaled replication study, register axis scoring with GPT-4o, and the non-Qwen rewriter control. Let me verify the exact count of experiments in the data—I'm seeing some overlap in my notes, so I should clarify whether there are 7 or 8 distinct experiments before finalizing the structure.\n\nNow I'm planning the paper's framing strategy. Since this is weaker evidence, I need to shift the narrative from claiming universality to positioning the CSD pipeline as a diagnostic tool. I'll acknowledge that only 2 out of 4 judges show significant formality bias, that GPT-4o's verbosity effect on Likert scales actually breaks the universality claim, and that scaled replication demonstrates Likert can reach significance at around n=350. I'm also considering how to present the GPT-4o verbosity findings in a way that's honest about what the data shows.\n\nFor the paper structure, I'll use a standard article class format with EMNLP-style conventions. I need seven tables covering the multi-judge formality results, cross-benchmark comparisons, Likert versus pairwise analysis, RATE control experiments, scaled replication findings, register evidence, and rewriter control results.\n\nNow I'm framing the narrative around the CSD pipeline as a diagnostic tool, with the Blindspot effect positioned as an observed phenomenon rather than the main focus, while elevating the GEE decomposition as the core contribution. The title should emphasize measurement-aware diagnosis of style bias in LLM judges, capturing how Likert scoring can fail and the implications of that failure.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3044,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11318,"cache_read_input_tokens":23823,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11318},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"344d64a3-a70b-4055-8c3e-46826b1f0ec1","uuid":"6cc9c19e-11e5-488a-b08f-45e712e12ad9"}
